{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVfq8A8eQaf1traBCGVJFZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"}]\n\nI found search results related to CoRL 2026, but the specific reviewer guidelines document for CoRL 2026 is not directly available in the current search results. However, I can provide you with what I found:\n\nThe search returned information about CoRL 2026 from the official CoRL website and OpenReview platform. The CoRL 2026 Conference is hosted on OpenReview, and CoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\nI did find detailed reviewer guidelines from a previous year (CoRL 2023), which covers key reviewing principles and criteria that are likely similar for CoRL 2026. The guidelines address relevance, asking whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, and whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both.\n\nFor the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking:\n1. The official CoRL website (corl.org)\n2. The OpenReview page for CoRL 2026 (openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference)\n\nThese platforms should have the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review forms for the 2026 conference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"b075302f-8522-4778-9a06-a80229d4a815","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:56:58.946Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019WdK1dFW2xZZGb5j1dYmF2","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"}]},"I found search results related to CoRL 2026, but the specific reviewer guidelines document for CoRL 2026 is not directly available in the current search results. However, I can provide you with what I found:\n\nThe search returned information about CoRL 2026 from the official CoRL website and OpenReview platform. The CoRL 2026 Conference is hosted on OpenReview, and CoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\nI did find detailed reviewer guidelines from a previous year (CoRL 2023), which covers key reviewing principles and criteria that are likely similar for CoRL 2026. The guidelines address relevance, asking whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, and whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both.\n\nFor the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking:\n1. The official CoRL website (corl.org)\n2. The OpenReview page for CoRL 2026 (openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference)\n\nThese platforms should have the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review forms for the 2026 conference."],"durationSeconds":4.825027071}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwigWB4NR3FFyGiw1gi7hL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"}]\n\nI found some relevant information about CoRL reviewing, though the search results include materials from different years of CoRL. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Review Information\n\nThe search results don't contain a specific document titled \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric.\" However, I did find:\n\n1. **CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation. Obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in reviewer scores.\n\n2. **CoRL 2024 Review Criteria**: Submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n3. **Scope Requirements**: All CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe official CoRL 2025 OpenReview page (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference) appears to be the primary source for the most current reviewer guidelines and review forms, but the detailed content isn't available in the search results. I'd recommend checking that OpenReview page directly for the specific 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"48cfd725-7cd2-4c23-ad74-52a2ba6556e4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:57:00.701Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BBjKjcL3t1yEf3YXnyznon","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"}]},"I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewing, though the search results include materials from different years of CoRL. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Review Information\n\nThe search results don't contain a specific document titled \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric.\" However, I did find:\n\n1. **CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation. Obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in reviewer scores.\n\n2. **CoRL 2024 Review Criteria**: Submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n3. **Scope Requirements**: All CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe official CoRL 2025 OpenReview page (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference) appears to be the primary source for the most current reviewer guidelines and review forms, but the detailed content isn't available in the search results. I'd recommend checking that OpenReview page directly for the specific 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric."],"durationSeconds":6.114163498999998}}
