{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6rkJ89tJzyVf87CCDzusY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:corl2023.org reviewer guidelines scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/papers\"},{\"title\":\"Workshops — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Detailed Program — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/detailed-program\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Presenters — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/instructions-for-presenters\"},{\"title\":\"Explore Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/explore-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Executive Board — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/about-corl-1\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Registration — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/registration\"}]\n\nI found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Based on the search results, here's what the guidelines cover regarding scoring criteria and reviewer expectations:\n\n## Key Reviewer Guidelines\n\n**Limitations Assessment:**\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and authors' honestly reported limitations should be treated kindly and with high appreciation. However, obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\n**Review Quality Standards:**\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views. Reviews should be as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n**Scoring Perspective:**\nThe guidelines provide important context for scoring decisions:\n- Publishing datasets/code, having theorems, or demonstrating on real robots are not strict policies and are not sufficient reasons for rejection by themselves.\n- A paper beating state-of-the-art is not a guarantee for acceptance, nor is not beating it a guarantee for rejection—what matters is novel perspectives, insights, and sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nThe reviewer guidelines page emphasizes constructive feedback and refers to resources from ICML and NeurIPS for additional guidance on writing quality reviews.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"5922c650-6442-4b62-86b4-ec4c5f54de57","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:57:11.722Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:corl2023.org reviewer guidelines scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018dKRXgavy7wdCQGnfRE3oP","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/papers"},{"title":"Workshops — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/workshops"},{"title":"CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/"},{"title":"Detailed Program — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/detailed-program"},{"title":"Instructions for Presenters — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/instructions-for-presenters"},{"title":"Explore Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/explore-papers"},{"title":"Executive Board — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/about-corl-1"},{"title":"Call for Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Registration — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/registration"}]},"I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Based on the search results, here's what the guidelines cover regarding scoring criteria and reviewer expectations:\n\n## Key Reviewer Guidelines\n\n**Limitations Assessment:**\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and authors' honestly reported limitations should be treated kindly and with high appreciation. However, obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\n**Review Quality Standards:**\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views. Reviews should be as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n**Scoring Perspective:**\nThe guidelines provide important context for scoring decisions:\n- Publishing datasets/code, having theorems, or demonstrating on real robots are not strict policies and are not sufficient reasons for rejection by themselves.\n- A paper beating state-of-the-art is not a guarantee for acceptance, nor is not beating it a guarantee for rejection—what matters is novel perspectives, insights, and sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nThe reviewer guidelines page emphasizes constructive feedback and refers to resources from ICML and NeurIPS for additional guidance on writing quality reviews."],"durationSeconds":6.010303005999998}}
