structions for CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.19309v1\"},{\"title\":\"My Paper Reviewing Load\",\"url\":\"https://danieltakeshi.github.io/2022/04/23/paper-reviewing-load/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found the official CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, I was unable to find the complete 1-10 scoring scale details in the search results. The official CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page (https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews) appears to be the authoritative source, but the search results only captured partial content from that page. \n\nTo access the full review scoring criteria and 1-10 rating scale for CoRL 2024, I recommend visiting the official instruction page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews, or checking the OpenReview portal at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024/Conference where the complete reviewer instructions may be available.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"e1cfd27f-0e75-4728-9b9f-6aedd0b4ef53","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:57:14.795Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale 1-10 review criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KT4NYNEo9thr6FosENvw16","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"t