{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TprYD9xsGqwvYXjgTDRtZj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Review Form Information for CoRL 2024\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **no complete review form is available**. The page titled \"Instruction for Reviews\" does not contain:\n\n- A scoring rubric with numbered dimensions\n- Numerical scales (e.g., 1-10 ratings)\n- Definitions of score levels\n- An acceptance rate\n\n## What IS Provided\n\nThe document outlines evaluation principles rather than a formal scoring instrument:\n\n**Review Focus:** Papers are assessed on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\" with consideration for \"potential for scientific and technological impact.\"\n\n**Desk Rejection Criteria** address formatting, anonymity violations, and scope alignment with robot learning research.\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications** specify minimum publication requirements in robotics and machine learning venues.\n\nTo obtain the actual review form with scoring dimensions and scales, you would need to access additional submission platform materials or contact the CoRL 2024 organizing committee directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"1e8d7919-c246-409b-97ed-0cb18e7d6e73","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:57:26.905Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134008,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Review Form Information for CoRL 2024\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **no complete review form is available**. The page titled \"Instruction for Reviews\" does not contain:\n\n- A scoring rubric with numbered dimensions\n- Numerical scales (e.g., 1-10 ratings)\n- Definitions of score levels\n- An acceptance rate\n\n## What IS Provided\n\nThe document outlines evaluation principles rather than a formal scoring instrument:\n\n**Review Focus:** Papers are assessed on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\" with consideration for \"potential for scientific and technological impact.\"\n\n**Desk Rejection Criteria** address formatting, anonymity violations, and scope alignment with robot learning research.\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications** specify minimum publication requirements in robotics and machine learning venues.\n\nTo obtain the actual review form with scoring dimensions and scales, you would need to access additional submission platform materials or contact the CoRL 2024 organizing committee directly.","durationMs":3836,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JXEUyHnKksYMwZ9avApVfW","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines - Scoring & Evaluation Criteria\n\nBased on the provided content, the document does **not specify numerical rating scales or explicit score meanings**. Instead, it outlines evaluation dimensions and qualitative guidance.\n\n## Evaluation Dimensions\n\nReviewers assess papers across six primary criteria:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\" Evaluate whether work represents novel combinations or clear differentiation from prior contributions.\n\n2. **Quality**: Technical soundness and whether \"claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results).\"\n\n3. **Clarity**: Writing quality and organization; papers should \"adequately inform the reader\" with sufficient detail for reproduction.\n\n4. **Significance**: Whether results represent important contributions likely to influence future research or practice.\n\n5. **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\" and whether the CoRL audience would find it valuable.\n\n6. **Limitations**: Papers must include a limitations section; \"honestly reported limitations\" should be treated favorably, while unreported flaws warrant stronger criticism.\n\n## Scoring Guidance\n\nThe guidelines emphasize **constructive, evidence-based reviews** avoiding common mistakes like unsupported novelty claims or demanding strict prerequisites (datasets, theorems, real robot testing).\n\nThe document references external resources (ICML and NeurIPS guidelines) for detailed scoring methodology but does not define a specific numerical scale within these reviewer guidelines."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"3f3f499f-faaa-45cf-b337-9453c0202996","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:57:30.020Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines - Scoring & Evaluation Criteria\n\nBased on the provided content, the document does **not specify numerical rating scales or explicit score meanings**. Instead, it outlines evaluation dimensions and qualitative guidance.\n\n## Evaluation Dimensions\n\nReviewers assess papers across six primary criteria:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\" Evaluate whether work represents novel combinations or clear differentiation from prior contributions.\n\n2. **Quality**: Technical soundness and whether \"claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results).\"\n\n3. **Clarity**: Writing quality and organization; papers should \"adequately inform the reader\" with sufficient detail for reproduction.\n\n4. **Significance**: Whether results represent important contributions likely to influence future research or practice.\n\n5. **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\" and whether the CoRL audience would find it valuable.\n\n6. **Limitations**: Papers must include a limitations section; \"honestly reported limitations\" should be treated favorably, while unreported flaws warrant stronger criticism.\n\n## Scoring Guidance\n\nThe guidelines emphasize **constructive, evidence-based reviews** avoiding common mistakes like unsupported novelty claims or demanding strict prerequisites (datasets, theorems, real robot testing).\n\nThe document references external resources (ICML and NeurIPS guidelines) for detailed scoring methodology but does not define a specific numerical scale within these reviewer guidelines.","durationMs":5746,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
