{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012AJwXoHP9rb2UATQN64LM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, now I have the OpenReview default scoring scale (1-10). CoRL uses OpenReview, so it likely uses this or a very similar scale. Let me also check the CoRL 2024 acceptance rate for calibration.\n\nFrom the search results, I found:\n- CoRL 2024 acceptance rate from Paper Copilot statistics page\n- OpenReview default form uses 1-10 scale\n\nLet me now construct my review. I have all the information I need:\n\n1. **Paper summary**: The paper presents a systematic RSA analysis of OpenVLA, finding that action-relevant representations come primarily from the vision encoder (SigLIP), not from LLM fine-tuning. \n\nThe core findings boil down to three main claims: vision encoder dominance in action-relevant representations, how LLM fine-tuning actually disrupts this structure, and the invariance properties across training and instruction variations.\n\n2. **Review context (imagined experiments)**: The paper covers 4 experiments:\n   - Per-layer RSA degradation curve (Appendix A)\n   - Random instruction control (Table 2)\n   - CKA verification (Table 3-4)\n   - LIBERO-Spatial benchmark extension (Table 5)\n\n3. **CoRL scoring**: 1-10 scale with the OpenReview defaults. CoRL focuses on robot learning, evaluating originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance.\n\nNow I'm setting up the review process by deploying two specialized reviewers in parallel—one to focus on methods and experimental rigor, the other on novelty and positioning relative to existing work—then I'll synthesize their perspectives in the roundtable discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":59260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2e3739-cf35-4bf4-84d7-4c529d34ab0f","uuid":"7cac04fd-2c09-4da7-b96e-60c6814773e7"}
